seriously before.

739
00:29:01.718 --> 00:29:05.099
Now I have to work double
just to get my credibility back.

740
00:29:10.067 --> 00:29:11.123
Hello. everyone.

741
00:29:11.208 --> 00:29:13.040
Thank you.Hey.

742
00:29:13.273 --> 00:29:16.025
Thanks again for giving me
the time to study for this Whipple.

743
00:29:16.110 --> 00:29:18.673
It's a lot.Mm-hmm.

744
00:29:18.757 --> 00:29:21.283
Look. Sam. this is
harder than I thought.

745
00:29:21.367 --> 00:29:23.328
It's like every time I'm
anywhere near Griff.

746
00:29:23.412 --> 00:29:25.906
all people think about
is. you know. that.

747
00:29:25.991 --> 00:29:28.388
Well. maybe you shouldn't
curl up on a bench with him

748
00:29:28.473 --> 00:29:29.692
and whisper.

749
00:29:31.160 --> 00:29:32.500
Sorry.

750
00:29:32.585 --> 00:29:34.243
I'm still thinking
about it. too.

751
00:29:36.023 --> 00:29:37.680
Tracy Reynolds is
having another heart attack.

752
00:29:37.764 --> 00:29:39.029
What?

753
00:29:43.634 --> 00:29:45.946
Push 150 of amio.

754
00:29:46.031 --> 00:29:47.527
Push 70 of roc
and 20 of etomidate.

755
00:29:47.612 --> 00:29:48.877
Do it.

756
00:29:48.961 --> 00:29:51.268
7-0 tube to me.

757
00:29:53.085 --> 00:29:54.305
Do you see that?

758
00:29:55.489 --> 00:29:57.509
Look like lesions. Viral?

759
00:29:57.594 --> 00:29:58.672
She's stable for now.

760
00:29:58.757 --> 00:30:00.310
Let's get a sample of
this to the lab ASAP.

761
00:30:00.394 --> 00:30:02.539
This might be what's
causing all her problems.

762
00:30:03.366 --> 00:30:04.743
Are you gonna be okay?

763
00:30:04.828 --> 00:30:06.459
Isn't your shift over?

764
00:30:07.446 --> 00:30:09.463
I'm fine. You can go.

765
00:30:09.952 --> 00:30:11.085
You don't look fine.

766
00:30:11.175 --> 00:30:12.571
And that makes sense.

767
00:30:12.656 --> 00:30:14.400
I mean. it's hard to
look at your mistakes.

768
00:30:14.485 --> 00:30:15.922
Own up to them.

769
00:30:16.989 --> 00:30:20.734
They call it a "fearless and
searching moral inventory."

770
00:30:21.500 --> 00:30:23.673
- Who calls it that?
- People in recovery.

771
00:30:23.758 --> 00:30:26.001
You know. like. accepting
the things you cannot change.

772
00:30:26.085 --> 00:30:28.081
Do you really think
appropriating 12-step mottos

773
00:30:28.166 --> 00:30:29.326
is gonna help me feel better?

774
00:30:29.732 --> 00:30:31.547
It helps me feel better.

775
00:30:32.091 --> 00:30:33.614
What do you mean?

776
00:30:34.658 --> 00:30:36.564
I got sober a couple months ago.

777
00:30:36.672 --> 00:30:38.978
right after Sam and I broke up.

778
00:30:39.063 --> 00:30:42.061
I made a lot of mistakes.

779
00:30:42.145 --> 00:30:44.799
And now I'm just trying to
do better one day at a time.

780
00:30:46.962 --> 00:30:48.445
I had no idea.

781
00:30:48.771 --> 00:30:50.557
I was good at hiding it.

782
00:30:52.133 --> 00:30:53.898
Nobody knows yet. It's new.

783
00:30:54.777 --> 00:30:56.056
I think if you can

784
00:30:56.141 --> 00:30:57.859
accept that you did all
you could for this patient.

785
00:30:57.943 --> 00:30:59.712
it'll be best for the
patients who still need you.

786
00:31:01.015 --> 00:31:02.368
Prelim path is in.

787
00:31:02.453 --> 00:31:04.298
Your guy had a malignant mass.

788
00:31:04.383 --> 00:31:07.391
It's pretty advanced
appendiceal cancer.

789
00:31:09.999 --> 00:31:11.785
His tissue was falling apart.

790
00:31:11.869 --> 00:31:13.309
That's why the
sutures wouldn't hold.

791
00:31:13.479 --> 00:31:15.136
Well. I still hit the iliac.

792
00:31:15.221 --> 00:31:18.703
Yeah. but if he hadn't had
cancer. you could have fixed it.

793
00:31:21.705 --> 00:31:23.362
I know that you don't
normally permit refunds.

794
00:31:23.446 --> 00:31:25.668
but this is a unique
circumstance. Uh...

795
00:31:25.752 --> 00:31:28.802
I'm not saying that the charge
was fraudulent. I'm just...

796
00:31:28.886 --> 00:31:30.630
"Cause"? Oh. come on.

797
00:31:30.714 --> 00:31:33.590
The cause is that no one needs
this many plastic butts. Bernie.

798
00:31:33.674 --> 00:31:35.940
This is for Tracy Reynolds. Can
you put a rush on those. please?

799
00:31:36.024 --> 00:31:38.446
Sir. I need you to
connect me to your boss.

800
00:31:38.531 --> 00:31:41.424
Sir? Sir?

801
00:31:41.508 --> 00:31:43.821
- Oh... 
- Looks like it's gonna be a late night.

802
00:31:43.906 --> 00:31:45.427
There's a Whipple in
the OR ahead of me.

803
00:31:45.511 --> 00:31:47.242
Hope
they got a good assist.

804
00:31:47.327 --> 00:31:48.996
Trulie. Which one is that?

805
00:31:49.080 --> 00:31:51.173
The hot one. third year. braids.

806
00:31:51.257 --> 00:31:52.827
Apparently she "assists" Griff.

807
00:31:52.911 --> 00:31:54.349
Oh.
right. the Griff girl.

808
00:31:54.433 --> 00:31:55.350
Explains
how she got the Whipple.

809
00:31:56.914 --> 00:31:58.397
Oh. boy.

810
00:31:58.481 --> 00:32:00.477
Oh. wow.

811
00:32:01.016 --> 00:32:02.843
I know you were not insinuating

812
00:32:02.928 --> 00:32:04.673
that a tremendously
talented surgeon

813
00:32:04.758 --> 00:32:07.884
got into an operation for any
reason other than her skill.

814
00:32:07.969 --> 00:32:08.974
No?

815
00:32:09.202 --> 00:32:11.845
If I can get past Dr. Trulie's
recent personal choices.

816
00:32:11.930 --> 00:32:12.934
you certainly can.

817
00:32:13.018 --> 00:32:15.048
And the only thing
you need to think.

818
00:32:15.133 --> 00:32:18.985
let alone say about her is
that she is an incredible doctor.

819
00:32:19.070 --> 00:32:20.637
And if she got an opportunity

820
00:32:20.721 --> 00:32:22.392
earlier in her career
than any of you.

821
00:32:22.477 --> 00:32:23.988
that is on your lack of skills.

822
00:32:24.157 --> 00:32:25.883
Not on her.

823
00:32:27.208 --> 00:32:28.209
Hmm?

824
00:32:43.632 --> 00:32:44.765
Labs got nothing.

825
00:32:44.993 --> 00:32:46.037
It's not a virus.

826
00:32:46.356 --> 00:32:47.838
Dr. Glass. can
you walk us through

827
00:32:47.922 --> 00:32:49.329
all of Tracy's cosmetic
procedures. please?

828
00:32:49.413 --> 00:32:51.821
Mm-hmm. Breast
augmentation. that was the start.

829
00:32:51.906 --> 00:32:53.366
Lower rhytidectomy after that.

830
00:32:53.450 --> 00:32:55.414
Blepharoplasty a year later.

831
00:32:55.499 --> 00:32:57.377
Laser skin resurfacing. she
gets that done fairly often.

832
00:32:57.461 --> 00:32:58.461
Where? Just her face?

833
00:32:58.789 --> 00:33:00.509
Mostly. Few times on her legs.

834
00:33:00.594 --> 00:33:02.723
Varicose vein removals.

835
00:33:02.807 --> 00:33:05.056
How often did you do her veins?

836
00:33:05.141 --> 00:33:07.143
More than most.

837
00:33:08.320 --> 00:33:09.511
It's not Tracy's age.

838
00:33:09.596 --> 00:33:11.384
It's a disease. She
was trying to smooth out

839
00:33:11.468 --> 00:33:12.992
her skin but it
wasn't age spots.

840
00:33:13.141 --> 00:33:14.953
Joint pain. She
said her knees hurt.

841
00:33:15.037 --> 00:33:17.868
Arthritis. headaches.
oral lesions.

842
00:33:17.952 --> 00:33:19.548
Superficial venous thrombosis.

843
00:33:19.633 --> 00:33:21.594
Tracy has Behcet's syndrome.

844
00:33:21.679 --> 00:33:23.742
Blood vessel
inflammation exacerbated

845
00:33:23.827 --> 00:33:24.875
by the estrogen supplements.

846
00:33:24.959 --> 00:33:26.149
None of which you caught

847
00:33:26.233 --> 00:33:27.890
while doing every
procedure under the sun.

848
00:33:28.046 --> 00:33:30.728
Oh. can it. Women get
work like this done every day.

849
00:33:30.813 --> 00:33:33.406
You want me to screen them all
for rare autoimmune disorders?

850
00:33:33.680 --> 00:33:34.758
She's right.

851
00:33:34.843 --> 00:33:36.022
Damn right I'm right.

852
00:33:36.245 --> 00:33:37.853
I didn't invent
beauty standards.

853
00:33:37.938 --> 00:33:40.461
even though they
do pay my mortgage.

854
00:33:40.799 --> 00:33:42.125
Standards.

855
00:33:42.263 --> 00:33:44.416
Start her on a gram
of methylprednisolone.

856
00:33:44.501 --> 00:33:46.157
That'll knock out the
inflammation for today.

857
00:33:46.241 --> 00:33:47.593
And then we are
gonna get her a team

858
00:33:47.677 --> 00:33:49.030
of specialists to
tailor her medications

859
00:33:49.114 --> 00:33:50.961
to her specific
symptoms. I have to go.

860
00:33:52.676 --> 00:33:54.376
Come on...

861
00:33:54.461 --> 00:33:56.514
That won't get it
here any faster.

862
00:33:56.599 --> 00:33:58.868
The devices.
They're for teaching. right?

863
00:33:58.953 --> 00:34:00.607
The contract specifically says

864
00:34:00.691 --> 00:34:02.821
that they represent a
"typical human body."

865
00:34:02.906 --> 00:34:04.871
except they are
all the exact same.

866
00:34:04.955 --> 00:34:06.525
They represent one body type.

867
00:34:06.609 --> 00:34:08.136
and it is young. thin and white.

868
00:34:08.220 --> 00:34:09.398
To call it "typical"

869
00:34:09.482 --> 00:34:10.977
is biased and discriminatory.

870
00:34:11.062 --> 00:34:12.793
And it implies that
there is a standard.

871
00:34:12.877 --> 00:34:14.001
And that is a standard
that my patient

872
00:34:14.085 --> 00:34:15.509
nearly killed herself
trying to live up to.

873
00:34:15.593 --> 00:34:17.913
Which nobody wants to argue
in the court of public opinion.

874
00:34:18.055 --> 00:34:19.538
Exactly!

875
00:34:19.622 --> 00:34:21.105
Which is why

876
00:34:21.189 --> 00:34:22.715
they are gonna let me
return all of those butts

877
00:34:22.799 --> 00:34:24.804
for a full refund.

878
00:34:24.888 --> 00:34:26.107
Hello.

879
00:34:28.109 --> 00:34:29.549
Wow.

880
00:34:29.633 --> 00:34:30.766
Boundaries.

881
00:34:30.850 --> 00:34:31.811
I mean. deep down. he knew

882
00:34:31.895 --> 00:34:33.465
what he was doing he was wrong.

883
00:34:33.549 --> 00:34:37.991
He just needed to hear it in
language he could understand.

884
00:34:38.075 --> 00:34:39.297
Now. of course. he
also needed a new set

885
00:34:39.381 --> 00:34:40.821
of golf clubs. but...

886
00:34:40.905 --> 00:34:42.692
That sounds like Griff.

887
00:34:42.776 --> 00:34:45.304
You know. he just
handed over the information

888
00:34:45.388 --> 00:34:49.047
Sam needed to
cancel the contracts.

889
00:34:49.131 --> 00:34:53.178
Asher. it was just...
That sounds less like him.

890
00:34:56.774 --> 00:35:00.041
Hey. Want to help me
pack up some butts?

891
00:35:00.533 --> 00:35:03.712
Only a fool would say
no to that.

892
00:35:03.796 --> 00:35:05.846
So. you called them and you
got them to give you a refund?

893
00:35:05.930 --> 00:35:07.326
Yeah. that's what they say.

894
00:35:07.410 --> 00:35:09.241
I'm still waiting on
the confirmation email.

895
00:35:09.325 --> 00:35:13.676
Well. so might you say
you butt-dialed them?

896
00:35:15.635 --> 00:35:17.205
No.

897
00:35:21.075 --> 00:35:23.168
I-I really needed that.

898
00:35:23.252 --> 00:35:24.951
Thank you.

899
00:35:25.035 --> 00:35:26.863
You always made
me laugh so much.

900
00:35:28.734 --> 00:35:29.997
I still could.

901
00:35:35.959 --> 00:35:37.439
How's Isan?

902
00:35:38.484 --> 00:35:40.359
Uh. he's... you know.

903
00:35:40.443 --> 00:35:42.534
it's a tough day. but
he's on the other side of it.

904
00:35:44.316 --> 00:35:46.277
Ugh. please. please. please.

905
00:35:46.361 --> 00:35:48.844
Ha!

906
00:35:48.928 --> 00:35:50.456
There's the email.

907
00:35:50.540 --> 00:35:52.716
Butts refunded in full.

908
00:35:53.716 --> 00:35:55.503
What is the company called?

909
00:35:55.587 --> 00:35:57.679
Uh. I
think it Emoti-Med.

910
00:35:57.763 --> 00:35:59.855
This says that the
$2 million refund

911
00:35:59.939 --> 00:36:01.728
is coming from "The
Waxman Corporation."

912
00:36:01.812 --> 00:36:03.932
Well. that's okay... it's
probably the parent company.

913
00:36:04.565 --> 00:36:06.340
No. no. no.

914
00:36:06.424 --> 00:36:07.994
Waxman?

915
00:36:08.078 --> 00:36:09.211
Oh. my God.

916
00:36:19.002 --> 00:36:21.313
Gerald Waxman.

917
00:36:24.486 --> 00:36:25.621
Oh. Sam.

918
00:36:25.711 --> 00:36:28.238
It was never about the devices.

919
00:36:28.323 --> 00:36:31.049
I walked right into his trap.

920
00:36:34.183 --> 00:36:36.081
Of course he didn't
care about the golf clubs.

921
00:36:36.166 --> 00:36:37.402
He just needed you to think

922
00:36:37.487 --> 00:36:39.449
that he wanted something.
that this was a trade.

923
00:36:39.534 --> 00:36:43.129
Gerald Waxman. multimillionaire
entrepreneur and philanthropist.

924
00:36:43.214 --> 00:36:46.269
Lakeshore's internal says
he's given a ton of donations.

925
00:36:46.354 --> 00:36:47.938
Way more than the
two million his devices cost.

926
00:36:48.022 --> 00:36:50.043
This month.
Waxman pledged to give

927
00:36:50.128 --> 00:36:51.985
Lakeshore a new donation.

928
00:36:52.685 --> 00:36:53.948
How much?

929
00:36:58.630 --> 00:37:00.590
$12 million.

930
00:37:07.574 --> 00:37:10.605
Waxie just called. Apparently.
he was counting on that sale

931
00:37:10.690 --> 00:37:12.529
to raise the profile of
his new company. so...

932
00:37:12.613 --> 00:37:16.378
when you canceled the
contract. he canceled the donation.

933
00:37:16.463 --> 00:37:19.879
You let Lakeshore lose
an eight-figure donation?

934
00:37:19.964 --> 00:37:21.667
And pinned it on me.

935
00:37:21.799 --> 00:37:24.714
I did tell you that the
lesson was gonna hurt.

936
00:37:24.799 --> 00:37:26.914
Hmm. But class is done.

937
00:37:26.999 --> 00:37:29.047
We can put all this behind
us and move forward.

938
00:37:29.131 --> 00:37:30.745
Here's what's gonna happen.

939
00:37:30.829 --> 00:37:31.854
I'll go down to storage

940
00:37:31.939 --> 00:37:33.698
where they boxed up
my stuff when I was shot

941
00:37:33.789 --> 00:37:36.794
and unconscious
and you stole my job.

942
00:37:36.878 --> 00:37:38.797
And somewhere
down there is a bottle

943
00:37:39.057 --> 00:37:41.582
of 50-year-old single malt.

944
00:37:41.666 --> 00:37:43.004
I'll take it to my office...

945
00:37:43.089 --> 00:37:44.448
It's Sam's office.

946
00:37:44.533 --> 00:37:46.831
You finish with your patients.
do what you have to do

947
00:37:47.454 --> 00:37:48.890
and come to see me.

948
00:37:50.240 --> 00:37:51.854
We'll have a drink.

949
00:37:52.925 --> 00:37:55.878
and negotiate your surrender.

950
00:37:58.885 --> 00:38:00.933
Thanks for sticking
around to chat.

951
00:38:01.165 --> 00:38:02.534
Always.

952
00:38:03.807 --> 00:38:06.534
Look. I respect what you said.

953
00:38:07.573 --> 00:38:09.218
but I can't sit this one out.

954
00:38:09.737 --> 00:38:11.275
I'm on Sam's side.

955
00:38:11.360 --> 00:38:15.081
Not because she needs
me. but because she doesn't.

956
00:38:15.980 --> 00:38:17.338
She is the better leader.

957
00:38:17.423 --> 00:38:18.906
Sam Griffith just made a mistake

958
00:38:18.991 --> 00:38:21.214
that cost Lakeshore
a lot of money.

959
00:38:21.299 --> 00:38:22.709
And I am sorry to hear that.

960
00:38:22.794 --> 00:38:24.065
but it doesn't change my mind.

961
00:38:24.150 --> 00:38:25.807
She will find a
way to turn the tide.

962
00:38:26.059 --> 00:38:27.448
You don't sound very neutral.

963
00:38:27.533 --> 00:38:28.584
And you are?

964
00:38:28.669 --> 00:38:29.935
Man. who are you kidding?

965
00:38:30.019 --> 00:38:31.459
All this golf with Griff?

966
00:38:31.544 --> 00:38:33.328
That's my business. son.

967
00:38:34.197 --> 00:38:36.156
And Sam is mine.

968
00:38:38.091 --> 00:38:39.400
Do what you want.

969
00:38:39.485 --> 00:38:41.970
But I can tell you
from experience.

970
00:38:42.055 --> 00:38:44.340
making alliances too
early in your career

971
00:38:44.425 --> 00:38:46.296
can lead to disaster.

972
00:38:49.905 --> 00:38:51.431
You are gonna
feel so much better

973
00:38:51.516 --> 00:38:52.840
once the immune-modulating
medication

974
00:38:52.924 --> 00:38:54.263
and the steroids kick in.

975
00:38:54.347 --> 00:38:56.131
And your heart will
be healthier. too.

976
00:38:57.087 --> 00:38:59.567
You must think I'm so stupid.

977
00:39:01.364 --> 00:39:04.346
Tracy. I'm one of two
women in my department.

978
00:39:06.865 --> 00:39:09.303
We're both battling how
we're perceived every day.

979
00:39:10.592 --> 00:39:12.244
Baldwin left.

980
00:39:13.269 --> 00:39:14.823
He said it wasn't my age.

981
00:39:14.908 --> 00:39:16.831
it was the fact that I lied.

982
00:39:16.921 --> 00:39:19.307
Can I offer you my
professional opinion?

983
00:39:19.392 --> 00:39:20.611
You know. as a doctor?

984
00:39:22.195 --> 00:39:24.588
Baldwin does not deserve you.

985
00:39:26.675 --> 00:39:28.620
You're probably right.

986
00:39:29.813 --> 00:39:34.081
But it's hard to find
someone. you know?

987
00:39:34.606 --> 00:39:37.534
Someone you really gel with.

988
00:39:39.161 --> 00:39:40.296
Yeah.

989
00:39:40.568 --> 00:39:41.832
I'm sorry.

990
00:39:50.273 --> 00:39:52.540
I'm gonna come check
on you later. okay?

991
00:39:52.736 --> 00:39:54.090
Okay.

992
00:40:00.133 --> 00:40:01.268
Hey.Hey.

993
00:40:01.353 --> 00:40:02.705
How was the Whipple?

994
00:40:02.790 --> 00:40:06.362
Slayed it. But that's
not why I'm here.

995
00:40:06.593 --> 00:40:10.035
Thank you for what
you said earlier.

996
00:40:10.119 --> 00:40:11.549
I know it's hardest for you

997
00:40:11.634 --> 00:40:14.117
with the whole...
me and him thing.

998
00:40:14.202 --> 00:40:15.997
When those idiots
were talking about you.

999
00:40:16.082 --> 00:40:18.065
I wasn't thinking about that.

1000
00:40:18.780 --> 00:40:21.260
I was just thinking
about my friend.

1001
00:40:23.262 --> 00:40:25.133
The wine thing?

1002
00:40:26.293 --> 00:40:29.081
Let's do that sooner than later.

1003
00:40:29.356 --> 00:40:31.260
I would love that.

1004
00:40:31.394 --> 00:40:32.747
Me. too.

1005
00:40:32.941 --> 00:40:34.293
Shall we go tonight?

1006
00:40:34.440 --> 00:40:37.604
Mm. unfortunately.
tonight I have to...

1007
00:40:39.190 --> 00:40:41.221
drink with someone else.

1008
00:40:44.973 --> 00:40:46.413
Excuse me.

1009
00:40:46.498 --> 00:40:48.155
Are you Dr. Isan Shah?

1010
00:40:48.240 --> 00:40:49.971
I am. Can I help you?

1011
00:40:50.064 --> 00:40:51.592
You've been named in
a wrongful death lawsuit.

1012
00:40:51.676 --> 00:40:53.057
You've been served.

1013
00:41:22.365 --> 00:41:23.802
Tell me how to hit him.

1014
00:41:25.076 --> 00:41:26.339
Happy to.

1015
00:41:28.283 --> 00:41:30.416
But like I said...

1016
00:41:31.283 --> 00:41:33.245
my help comes with a price.

1017
00:41:33.343 --> 00:41:37.518
Rhonda. if it's less
than $12 million...

1018
00:41:39.551 --> 00:41:41.029
I'm in.

